  "brief": [
    {
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "A retailer studies satisfaction (SYNTHETIC data). The starter declares every construct reflective. Decide from the definitions below how each construct must be measured and correct the model."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**F – Service convenience (index):** defined by management as the combination of f1 opening hours, f2 store location, f3 online booking and f4 parking. A store can score high on one and low on another.",
        "**X – Staff friendliness:** x1 \"Staff were friendly\", x2 \"Staff were courteous\", x3 \"Staff were pleasant to deal with\".",
        "**Y – Satisfaction:** y1–y4, four statements of overall satisfaction with the store.",
        "Hypotheses: F → Y and X → Y."
      ]
    }
  ],
